{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about or consider an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer; after the offer it may weigh only specified convictions and must perform an individualized assessment before withdrawing the offer.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider, excluding dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; inquiries about methamphetamine manufacture on federally assisted housing premises and lifetime sex-offender registration.","penalty":"Director may impose up to $1,000 for a first violation, up to $5,000 for one prior violation and up to $10,000 for two or more prior violations, and require compliance measures.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure and return","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether it reviews criminal history and that the applicant may submit evidence of record inaccuracies or rehabilitation. On a violation, the director may order the fee returned.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider, excluding dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1)   Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history; and (2)   A statement that the applicant, pursuant to subsection a. of this section, may provide evidence demonstrating inaccuracies within the applicant’s criminal record or evidence of rehabilitation or other mitigating factors.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after successful appeal","requirement":"If a court overturns the director's order and finds the housing provider did not violate the act, the provider may evict a person housed under that order, giving at least 45 days' notice.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider, excluding dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"]},"exemptions":"Dwelling units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"P.L. 2021, c. 110","quoted_span":"a determination that the housing provider did not violate the provisions of this act as evidenced by such successful appeal shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction;","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
